% Macros shared by this bank's LaTeX output.
%
% The .sty counterpart of bank_helpers.py, and yours to edit for the same
% reason: it ships nearly empty so you have somewhere to put what your bank
% needs, rather than discovering later that there was nowhere.
%
% WHAT BELONGS HERE
%
% Commands and packages your *content* cannot compile without. If a generator
% emits \myNumeral{7}, or a template writes \degreesign, the definition goes
% here. So does any \usepackage the content depends on.
%
% The test is whether the document breaks without it. \usepackage{hieroglf},
% because an outcome sets Egyptian numerals, belongs here: without it the file
% does not compile. \geometry{margin=1in} does not -- the document compiles
% fine and merely looks different, which makes it a styling choice and the
% business of whatever is producing the page.
%
% Keeping that line matters. This file is loaded by two very different
% documents, and anything in it has to be safe in both.
%
% WHO LOADS IT
%
%   * Figure compilation. wrapper/tikz.py builds each .tikz into a PNG inside a
%     standalone document. If you add a tikz_preamble.tex to your bank root, it
%     replaces the default one, and it should \usepackage{bank_helpers} so your
%     figures can use the same commands your prose does.
%
%   * Printing, if you use the print tool. Its theme loads this file alongside
%     its own layout package.
%
% Because a figure is a borderless standalone with no page, page-level settings
% put here will either do nothing or break the figure build. That is the
% practical reason for the rule above, not just tidiness.
%
% Nothing loads this file for the HTML viewer: the browser renders maths with
% KaTeX and never sees LaTeX macros. A command defined here has no effect on
% screen, so content that needs to *look* different in each medium wants a
% SpaTeXt element instead -- see <glyphs> and <nobreak> in CODEBASE_NOTES.md.

\ProvidesPackage{bank_helpers}

